# What the files of this directory are, for update.sh (which reads it from the release's orch-deploy bundle).
#
# generation: the generation of the files in this release. It is raised when any file of the main set differs from the
#   latest published release's; a release's gate refuses a candidate that changes the set and leaves the number.
# minimum: the oldest generation of the main set the programs of this release work with. It is raised by hand, only when a
#   release needs a change in these files, and the release notes give the reason: an update whose kept or old set is older
#   stops before it stops anything.
# set main: the files that must agree with each other; replaced whole when every member equals a published file.
# file: what a published release shipped (tag, generation, SHA-256, path below deploy/). Packaging adds a release's own
#   rows to the copy in its bundle; once a release is published, `python3 .github/scripts/release_contract.py
#   record-published --tag vX.Y.Z --revision <tag>` adds them here. Nothing under config/ is listed: it is never touched.
format 1
generation 1
minimum 1
set main compose.yml compose.frontend-https.yml nginx.conf frontend.sh frontend-csp.sh postgres/Dockerfile hosts/runtimes/common.sh hosts/runtimes/gvisor.sh hosts/runtimes/kata.sh
